# Wayboxd Core Standards

## Project structure

```
src/
  ├── app/
  │   ├── _util/          # Utility helpers (password, etc.)
  │   ├── api/            # API route handlers under (controller)/
  │   │   └── model/      # Request/response types
  │   └── service/        # Business logic + email templates (no try-catch here)
  └── proxy.ts            # Auth proxy (Next.js 16; excludes public/auth API paths)
prisma/                   # Schema and migrations
```

## TypeScript

- Use English for all code and documentation
- Always declare types; avoid `any`
- Naming: PascalCase (types/classes), camelCase (functions/vars), kebab-case (files/dirs), UPPERCASE (constants/env)
- Keep functions focused; use early returns
- Null safety: prefer `obj?.property`, `obj?.value ?? defaultValue`

## Logging

- Avoid `console.log` in route handlers and services
- Add structured logging via a shared logger when the project introduces one

## Code quality

- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run format:check` before committing
- Husky pre-commit runs `lint-staged` (Prettier on staged files, auto-re-staged); pre-push runs build

## Agent context

- Domain map: `docs/agent/domain-map.md`
- Team memory (decisions, gotchas): `docs/agent/memory.md`
- Workflows: use skills in `.agents/skills/` (`new-api-route`, `new-api-client`, `new-service`, `new-email-template`, `new-prisma-migration`)
